  "portal_description": "OpenShift Enterprise includes the following functionality:\n\nPolyglot Language Support \u2013 OpenShift Enterprise includes built-in support for Java, Ruby, Python, PHP and Perl programming languages.  Developers can choose the language that suits their own skills, or the requirements of the job.\n\nMultiple Interfaces \u2013 OpenShift Enterprise also allows developers to work the way they want to work by providing multiple interfaces to the PaaS. Developers can use a rich set of command-line tools, a powerful web console, which can be accessed on multiple devices, or an Eclipse-based Integrated Development Environment, such as JBoss Developer Studio.\n\nAutoscaling \u2013 OpenShift Enterprise can scale applications automatically to handle increased traffic and demand on the application.\n\nApplication Portability \u2013 OpenShift Enterprise is built with standard language and middleware run-times so that any application written on OpenShift can easily be moved to another environment that supports similar programming languages. OpenShift Enterprise provides developers with the flexibility to choose their environment.\n\nOpen Source \u2013 OpenShift Enterprise is based on open source technologies.  The OpenShift PaaS itself is derived from the OpenShift Origin open source project.\n\nBuilt on Red Hat Technologies \u2013 OpenShift Enterprise is built on Red Hat's time-tested and enterprise class open source technology stack, including Red Hat Enterprise Linux and JBoss Enterprise Application Platform.",
